#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:739
msgctxt "/Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:739"
msgid "`v0.9.0` - Introduced."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:741
msgid ""
"`ptool.run_shell(command)` executes `command` through the configured shell."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:743
msgid "`command` (string, required): Shell script or shell command text."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:744
msgid "Returns: The same result table as `ptool.run(...)`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:746
msgctxt "/Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:746"
msgid "Behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:748
msgid "The shell command comes from `ptool.config({ shell = ... })`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:749
msgid "If `shell` is not configured, `ptool.run_shell(...)` uses `\"bash\"`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:750
msgid "`ptool.run_shell(command)` is equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:756
msgctxt "/Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:756"
msgid ""
"The default `echo`, `check`, `confirm`, and `retry` values still come from "
"`ptool.config({ run = { ... } })`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:758
msgid ""
"If you need per-call `options` such as `cwd`, `env`, `stdin`, or `stdout = "
"\"capture\"`, call `ptool.run(...)` directly with the shell and `-c`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:761
msgctxt "/Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/core.md:761"
